-- title:
--   Zeroth shells outside S and the S-part torus measure
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and $c \in [0,\infty]$. The hypothesis `hc` asserts an Iwasawa-type disintegration with constant $c$: for every measurable subset $D$ of the idèle group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ that is a fundamental domain for the subgroup of principal idèles (the image of $K^\times$ under `Units.map` of the structure map) with respect to the Haar measure [`NumberField.Idele.idelicHaar K`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L391), and every measurable $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to [0,\infty]$ satisfying $f(xg) = f(g)$ for all $x$ in `rationalCentreUnipotent K` (the subgroup generated by the scalar matrices with entries in $K^\times$ together with the adelic upper unipotents) and all $g$, the integral of $f \circ \mathrm{out}$ over the orbit quotient by `rationalCentreUnipotent K`, taken with respect to `rationalCentreUnipotentQuotientMeasure K`, equals $c \int_{z \in D} \int_t \int_k f(z \cdot \mathrm{diag}(t,1) \cdot k)\,\|t\|^{-1}$, where $k$ runs over the adelic maximal compact (matrices integral at every finite place with row-isometric archimedean components) with its Haar measure, $t$ over the idèles with `idelicHaar`, and $\|t\|$ is the idèle norm given by the distributive Haar character. Given in addition a finite set $S$ of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, such a $D$, and such an $f$, the conclusion states that restricting the quotient integral to those classes $q$ whose representative $q.\mathrm{out}$ lies in `RankinSelberg.shellZeroOutside K S`, i.e. satisfies $|\det g|_v = \max(|g_{10}|_v, |g_{11}|_v)^2$ at every finite place $v \notin S$, yields the same triple integral with the measure on $t$ replaced by [`NumberField.Idele.sPartMeasure K S`](def/NumberField_IdeleProductMeasure.html#L458), the pushforward under $t \mapsto \mathrm{part}_S(t)$ of `idelicHaar` restricted to the idèles that are units outside $S$.
--
--   This is the $S$-part of the Iwasawa disintegration of the quotient integral over $Z(K)N(\mathbb{A}) \backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$: cutting the quotient integral down to the zeroth Iwasawa shells at all finite places outside $S$ replaces the full torus Haar measure by its $S$-and-infinity part. It feeds the Rankin–Selberg unfolding step [`AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.lintegral_sPart_quotientIntegrand_eq_mul_lintegral_torus_and_sPartIntegral_eq`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.lintegral_sPart_quotientIntegrand_eq_mul_lintegral_torus_and_sPartIntegral_eq).
